    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task: reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone already belongs to another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges made (following existing Spring conventions in the codebase):\n\n1. **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** (new, in `rest/advice`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `InvalidFieldsException` pattern, signaling a telephone conflict.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateTelephoneException` that returns a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the other handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the telephone is normalized to its ten-digit form (the form actually stored), it calls a new `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` helper that scans existing owners via `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and throws the exception on a match. The check runs on the normalized value, so `04 0000 0011` and `(040) 000-0011` collide correctly.\n\nTest results: the two new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expecting 409, and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` expecting 2xx) both pass, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures/errors.",
